        "content": "<p>When managing some PRs to mathlib, I found the following phenomenon:<br>\nFor namespace <code>A B</code> and a declaration <code>B.foo</code>, in namespace <code>A</code> we open <code>B</code>, <code>foo</code> can represent <code>B.foo</code> if and only if the namespace <code>A.B</code> doesn't exist. Is this a feature or something else? Although open <code>B</code> outside <code>A</code> works, but I want to know (:</p>",
